# OPM Troubleshooting

Go-based OLM operator troubleshooting toolkit for OpenShift. Pure Go replacement for `opm render` + `jq` + `skopeo inspect`.

## Stack

- Go 1.26.3+, build tag `containers_image_openpgp` (no gpgme C dependency)
- `operator-registry` for FBC rendering, `go-containerregistry` for bundle inspection
- `chromem-go` vector store for RAG, `mcp-go` v0.56.0 for MCP server
- `k8s.io/client-go` for live cluster mode, `go-sqlite3` for metadata persistence

## Binaries (built to `bin/` via `make build`)

- `catalog-bundle-inspect` — OLM catalog bundle inspector
- `batch-validate` — batch operator validation
- `telco-diagnose` — telco production diagnosis (27 operators)
- `opm-diagnose` — unified diagnostics (live cluster + must-gather)
- `ocp-rag-server` — MCP server exposing 8 RAG tools
- `ocp-rag-ingest` / `ocp-rag-query` — RAG ingestion and query CLIs

## Commands

- `make build` — build all binaries
- `make test` — run unit tests
- `make lint` — run golangci-lint
- `DOCKER_CONFIG=/path/to/config` — registry auth for private catalogs

## MCP

The `ocp-rag` MCP server provides 8 tools for OpenShift troubleshooting. Use `troubleshoot_operator` for broad diagnosis, then drill down with `search_docs`, `search_operator_code`, `search_known_issues`, etc.
